Brief Description 
———————————
This library trains and tests a residual network (resnet18) for the purpose of classification of ocean features.


Source of Dataset
————————————
The ocean features are the ones detailed in the paper:

Wang, Chen, et al. "A labelled ocean SAR imagery dataset of ten geophysical phenomena from Sentinel‐1 wave mode." Geoscience Data Journal 6.2 (2019): 105-115.

The dataset contains 10 ocean features.


Training
————————————
The train.py file needs to be run in order to train the model. Following is an example of a way to run the file:

Train from beginning using command lines: python3 train.py 50 /Users/SC/Desktop/wang/data/ mps --resume_train False --save_dir train1 --batch_size 128

Resume training using command lines : python3 train.py 50  /Users/SC/Desktop/wang/data/ mps --resume_train True --save_dir train1 --batch_size 128

50 denotes the number of epochs. Note that it controls the number of epochs for second part of the model training. The first part is trained with 20 epochs by default. Thus if you put 50 then total 70 epochs would be run!

Here “ /Users/SC/Desktop/wang/data/“ denotes the absolute path of the directory containing the full dataset (containing train and val datasets, but not the test datasets). A sample data folder containing a few images in each class is put here for your reference. 
 
mps denotes that kind of compute being used is metal performance shaders. Type cuda if you are using Nvidia GPU and type cpu if you do not.

train1 denotes the name of the folder where the model and curves would be saved. 


Testing
————————————
The test.py file in the tests folder can be run for evaluating the trained model on a sample image.


Folder Structure
————————————
## Folder Structure

```
├── src/
│   ├── data_loader.py      # Data loading and preprocessing functions
│   ├── models_src.py       # Model architecture
│   ├── utils.py            # Utility functions
│   ├── train.py            # Training loop and logic
│
├── models/
│   └── trial/              # Contains .pth models and checkpoints
│
├── tests/
│   └── test.py             # Unit tests
│
├── README.md               # Project overview and instructions
│
├── requirements.txt        # Library and Python version details
│
├── data/                   # Subset of the dataset used for training
│   ├── F/  # Pure Ocean Waves (POW)
│   ├── G/  # Wind Streaks (WS)
│   ├── H/  # Micro Convective Cells (MCC)
│   ├── I/  # Rain Cells (RC)
│   ├── J/  # Biological Slicks (BS)
│   ├── K/  # Sea Ice (SI)
│   ├── L/  # Ice Bergs (IB)
│   ├── M/  # Low Wind Areas (LWA)
│   ├── N/  # Atmospheric Fronts (AF)
│   └── O/  # Ocean Fronts (OF)
```

